# AlertDialog

> Lede 0.8.1's docs for AlertDialog, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/alert-dialog.md

A modal that asks before an action that needs a second thought, with Cancel and a confirm Button. Focus opens on confirm, or on Cancel for a critical action, and Escape cancels.

Experimental: its props can change in a minor release, which the CHANGELOG names. An item is experimental for the release that adds it, and stable once a release ships it unchanged.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/alert-dialog
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), [`button`](button.md) and [`theme-provider`](theme-provider.md), and the npm packages `@base-ui/react@^1.9.0`. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.8.1/alert-dialog.json.

