## Props

A modal that asks before an action that needs a second thought: Base UI AlertDialog, a `role="alertdialog"` named by its title and described by its description, with Cancel and a confirm Button. Focus opens on the confirm button, or on Cancel when `tone` is `'critical'`, stays inside while it’s open and returns to where it was. Escape cancels, and a press outside does nothing.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | The question, such as “Delete edge-sfo-2?”. It names the dialog. |
| `description` | `React.ReactNode` |  | What happens if the person confirms, such as “Its 3 deploy runs go too. You can’t undo this.” It describes the dialog. |
| `confirmLabel` (required) | `string` |  | The confirm button’s label, a verb for what it does, such as “Delete”. |
| `cancelLabel` | `string` |  | The cancel button’s label. Default “Cancel”. |
| `tone` | `ToneSubset<'primary' \| 'critical'>` | `primary` | `'critical'` for an action that destroys something: the confirm button turns critical, and focus opens on Cancel. Default `'primary'`. |
| `onConfirm` (required) | `() => void` |  | Runs when the person confirms, before the dialog closes. |
| `trigger` | `React.ReactElement` |  | The control that opens the dialog, such as a Button. Leave it unset and pass `open` to open it from elsewhere, such as a row action. |
| `open` | `boolean` |  | Whether the dialog is open, for a parent that controls it. |
| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether the dialog is open at first. Default `false`. |
| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` |  | Called with the new state when the dialog opens or closes, by a button, Escape or the trigger. |
| `finalFocus` | `React.RefObject<HTMLElement \| null>` |  | Where focus goes when the dialog closes. Default: the trigger, or the control that had focus when it opened. Pass an element when that control is gone, such as a row the action deleted. |
| `className` | `string` |  | Classes for the dialog’s box. |

